The Operating Environment Philosophy defines the institutional principles that govern how the COREI Operating Environment shall exist, behave, evolve, and support the institution.

Unlike architecture, which defines structure, philosophy defines the enduring operational principles that every implementation decision must respect.

The philosophy is permanent.

Technologies may change.

Implementations may evolve.

