2. Mission

Establish the foundational operational beliefs that transform COREI from software into an Institutional Intelligent Operating Environment.

Every repository, runtime, workspace, terminal, service, and operator interaction shall align with these principles.

3. Philosophy Statement

COREI is not an application.

COREI is not a dashboard.

COREI is not a terminal.

COREI is not a collection of services.

COREI is an Institutional Intelligent Operating Environment.

Everything exists because the Operating Environment provides existence.

Nothing operates independently.

Everything operates within COREI.

4. First Principle — Environment Before Applications

Applications are temporary.

The Operating Environment is permanent.

The institution does not operate applications.

The institution operates an environment.

Every capability shall therefore become a native capability of the Operating Environment rather than an independent application.

5. Second Principle — One Institutional Reality

The institution shall experience one operational reality.

Not:

separate dashboards
separate terminals
separate applications
disconnected services

